---
// Case H — Forest & Commodity Watch. Skeleton until the pipeline lands.
// Spec: docs/spec-forest-watch.html (H5 dashboard anatomy).
import "../styles/tokens.css";
---
<html lang="en" data-case="forest" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Forest &amp; Commodity Watch</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main style="min-height:100vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center;gap:16px;padding:0 6vw;">
      <span style="font-family:var(--font-data);font-size:0.72rem;letter-spacing:0.14em;color:var(--accent);">CASE H · SCAFFOLDED · PIPELINE PENDING</span>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.2rem);margin:0;line-height:1.1;">Forest &amp; Commodity Watch</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);max-width:36rem;margin:0;">Where Global Forest Watch stops: weekly radar
      deforestation alerts clustered into events and linked to concessions, oil-palm plantations and mills —
      so a disturbance becomes a supply-chain question, not just a pixel.</p>
      <!-- TODO per spec H5: hero "canopy to burn" — a province's alert clusters igniting week by week
           (canvas 2-D fallback: pre-rendered weekly frames on a 2-D canvas with a scrubber) →
           chapters (two decades of loss · the alerts · linked or unlinked — the concession share ·
           the mills) → explore (cluster map + concession/mill layers, before/after Sentinel-2 chips,
           filters) → methodology. Map rule (WebGL off): try MapLibre, catch → 2-D canvas, as in
           cases/nightlights-pulse/web. -->
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
